{"name":"Dulcinea","hex":"#d6d4e6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Dulcinea","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mistress; a sweetheart."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Dulcinea"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dulcinea (The Expanse)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Dulcinea\" is the series premiere of the American science fiction television series The Expanse. It originally aired on Syfy in the United States on December 14, 2015. The episode was written by Mark Fergus and Hawk Ostby and directed by Terry McDonough, and is based on the first chapters of James S. A. Corey's novel Leviathan Wakes, the first novel in The Expanse novel series."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dulcinea_(The_Expanse)"},{"title":"Dulcinea (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Dulcinea is an album by Toad the Wet Sprocket released in 1994. It is their fourth studio album with Columbia Records and the follow-up to their popular album Fear, which was released in 1991. Two songs from Dulcinea charted on the Modern Rock and Mainstream Rock charts: \"Fall Down\" and \"Something's Always Wrong\". Dulcinea was RIAA Certified Gold on September 1, 1994, and Platinum on July 31, 1995."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/af/Dulcinea_%28album%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dulcinea_(album)"},{"title":"Dulcinea del Toboso","blocks":[{"text":"Dulcinea del Toboso is a fictional character who is unseen in Miguel de Cervantes's novel Don Quixote. Don Quixote believes he must have a lady to whom to direct his courtly love and homage, according to his understanding, nurtured by chivalric literature, that the knightly life requires it.\nAs he does not have one, he invents her, making her the very model of female perfection: \"[h]er name is Dulcinea, her country El Toboso, a village of La Mancha, her rank must be at least that of a princess, since she is my queen and lady, and her beauty superhuman, since all the impossible and fanciful attributes of beauty which the poets apply to their ladies are verified in her; for her hairs are gold, her forehead Elysian fields, her eyebrows rainbows, her eyes suns, her cheeks roses, her lips coral, her teeth pearls, her neck alabaster, her bosom marble, her hands ivory, her fairness snow, and what modesty conceals from sight such, I think and imagine, as rational reflection can only extol, not compare\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Monumento_a_Cervantes_%28Madrid%29_09.jpg/330px-Monumento_a_Cervantes_%28Madrid%29_09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dulcinea_del_Toboso"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Hawk_Ostby%2C_at_the_Hugo_Awards_Ceremony%2C_Worldcon%2C_Helsinki.jpg/500px-Hawk_Ostby%2C_at_the_Hugo_Awards_Ceremony%2C_Worldcon%2C_Helsinki.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Hawk_Ostby%2C_at_the_Hugo_Awards_Ceremony%2C_Worldcon%2C_Helsinki.jpg/1280px-Hawk_Ostby%2C_at_the_Hugo_Awards_Ceremony%2C_Worldcon%2C_Helsinki.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Hawk_Ostby%2C_at_the_Hugo_Awards_Ceremony%2C_Worldcon%2C_Helsinki.jpg/500px-Hawk_Ostby%2C_at_the_Hugo_Awards_Ceremony%2C_Worldcon%2C_Helsinki.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hawk Ostby, along with his writing partner Mark Fergus, wrote the first episode.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHawk_Ostby%2C_at_the_Hugo_Awards_Ceremony%2C_Worldcon%2C_Helsinki.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/El_Toboso_Monumento_a_D._Quijote_y_Dulcinea.jpg/500px-El_Toboso_Monumento_a_D._Quijote_y_Dulcinea.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/El_Toboso_Monumento_a_D._Quijote_y_Dulcinea.jpg/500px-El_Toboso_Monumento_a_D._Quijote_y_Dulcinea.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Monument to Don Quixote and Dulcinea, Castilla-La Mancha, Spain.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEl_Toboso_Monumento_a_D._Quijote_y_Dulcinea.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Charles_Robert_Leslie_%281794-1859%29_-_Dulcinea_del_Toboso_-_FA.131%28O%29_-_Victoria_and_Albert_Museum.jpg/500px-Charles_Robert_Leslie_%281794-1859%29_-_Dulcinea_del_Toboso_-_FA.131%28O%29_-_Victoria_and_Albert_Museum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Charles_Robert_Leslie_%281794-1859%29_-_Dulcinea_del_Toboso_-_FA.131%28O%29_-_Victoria_and_Albert_Museum.jpg/500px-Charles_Robert_Leslie_%281794-1859%29_-_Dulcinea_del_Toboso_-_FA.131%28O%29_-_Victoria_and_Albert_Museum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dulcinea del Toboso by Charles Robert Leslie, 1839","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACharles_Robert_Leslie_(1794-1859)_-_Dulcinea_del_Toboso_-_FA.131(O)_-_Victoria_and_Albert_Museum.jpg"}],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Grey heron (00129p)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg/500px-Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg","ratio":0.8691693290734824,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_heron_(00129p).jpg","share":0.52375},{"title":"006477 - El Toboso (7623162468)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/006477_-_El_Toboso_%287623162468%29.jpg/500px-006477_-_El_Toboso_%287623162468%29.jpg","ratio":1.5,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:006477_-_El_Toboso_(762316